The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which meant it was returning the second word instead of the first word. This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail because `first_word('hello world')` returned `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- `test_single` to error because `first_word('solo')` tried to access index 1 in a list with only one element

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split list.
